cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Precedent, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Precedent: human-approved operating rules and deterministic action gates for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  Precedent turns how a team already works into operating rules that AI agents follow.
  It mines question-and-answer threads from team chat (WhatsApp, Slack, JSONL) into draft
  rules grounded in the source messages, requires a person to approve every change, and
  gates each agent action through deterministic checks outside the model (coverage,
  judgement, grounding, risk-tiered confidence, risk), returning act, needs-approval or
  escalate. A second, execution gate re-checks each step and the result after the action is
  done, and halts a running action that goes beyond its decision, recording which rule, which
  run and who halted it. Every escalation becomes a draft rule and a regression test; drift detection
  flags stale, overridden, unused and duplicate rules. It runs as a Python library, CLI,
  MCP server, or compiles to Agent Skills and AGENTS.md.
